      "attestations": [
        {
          "text": "CH'ÊN Wên-shu 陳文述 (T. 退庵, 雲伯, H. 碧城外史, 頤道先生, 蓮可居士, 秦亭山樵), 1775–1840, official and poet, was a native of Ch'ien-t'ang (Hangchow). Even as a youth he gained recognition as a poet, and the designation Êr Ch'ên 二陳 or \"The Two Ch'êns\" was given to him and his cousin, Ch'ên Hung-shou 陳鴻壽 (T. 頌文, 子恭, 翼庵, H. 曼生, 1768–1822), who was a poet, a painter, and a calligrapher.",
